WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:02.960
<b>Year 2 Class 3</b>

00:01.750 --> 00:06.790
Ichikawa, can you be student rep and read
a farewell address to our graduating class?

00:07.000 --> 00:08.670
What? Absolutely not.

00:09.630 --> 00:11.500
What? No way, that's awesome!

00:11.500 --> 00:15.500
Y-yeah, but this is something
an honors student should do.

00:15.750 --> 00:18.130
Someone like Ishimuro or Hara.

00:18.380 --> 00:19.540
What about me?

00:19.540 --> 00:20.920
Be my guest.

00:21.670 --> 00:23.460
A farewell speech? Why not you?

00:23.460 --> 00:24.960
You've got good grades.

00:24.960 --> 00:26.960
Got the second highest grade on our finals and all.

00:26.960 --> 00:28.750
Wait, that's amazing! You did?

00:28.750 --> 00:30.000
You didn't hear?

00:30.000 --> 00:32.920
I was all happy about doing a little better, and then...

00:33.830 --> 00:36.540
That all? I'm second from the top.

00:38.290 --> 00:39.500
You should do it!

00:39.500 --> 00:40.830
Ichikawa's giving a farewell speech?

00:40.830 --> 00:41.920
Hilarious.

00:41.920 --> 00:43.580
This isn't about grades though...

00:44.710 --> 00:45.830
Okay, okay.

00:45.830 --> 00:48.000
I'm not trying to force you or anything.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.170
But, we have a rehearsal tomorrow
and no one has taken the role yet.

01:02.330 --> 01:04.960
Just until you find someone, then.

01:05.290 --> 01:08.750
If it's just for the rehearsal, fine...

02:45.670 --> 02:51.130
Next, a farewell address from student
representative Kyotaro Ichikawa.

02:57.330 --> 02:59.830
I should have said no...

03:04.630 --> 03:05.540
Farewell.

03:05.540 --> 03:08.500
The day your journey begins has come.

03:08.500 --> 03:11.880
Despite the harsh cold,
the rays of spring fall warm upon us now.

03:11.880 --> 03:14.670
I want to wish all of you celebrating
your graduation today, congratulations.

03:14.670 --> 03:16.080
Can't hear a word...

03:16.080 --> 03:17.460
On behalf of all of us here,

03:17.460 --> 03:18.880
Basically whispering...
I wish you all the best.<b></b>

03:19.830 --> 03:21.580
All of us came to this school
not knowing what to expect,

03:21.580 --> 03:22.790
and you welcomed us with open arms.

03:23.080 --> 03:23.920
Who's that?

03:23.920 --> 03:25.250
He's a nervous wreck!

03:28.170 --> 03:30.880
You sure sounded quiet up there.

03:30.880 --> 03:34.000
Trouble with the sound system, I guess.

03:34.170 --> 03:35.460
I died out there.

03:38.420 --> 03:39.670
Good try out there.

03:40.380 --> 03:43.080
I-I bet they'll look for someone else now.

03:43.080 --> 03:44.250
And fine by me.

03:44.250 --> 03:45.670
Let's practice. C'mon!

03:45.670 --> 03:46.920
Huh? Wha?!

03:47.500 --> 03:49.710
C'mon, I'm not gonna do this!

03:49.710 --> 03:52.750
I take voice lessons and stuff, don't worry.

03:53.000 --> 03:55.210
Now focus on your diaphragm.

03:56.380 --> 03:58.290
The diaphragm is higher up.

04:04.920 --> 04:06.790
In closing...

04:06.790 --> 04:11.000
I hope that you all remain in
good health and accomplish great things,

04:11.000 --> 04:12.500
and from all of us, farewell.

04:12.500 --> 04:15.670
Wow! That was much better!

04:16.670 --> 04:18.710
Standing straight like this is exhausting.

04:19.000 --> 04:20.330
That was great!

04:20.330 --> 04:22.710
Must be 'cause you're second in our grade.

04:23.670 --> 04:26.170
You're the one who gave me voice lessons.

04:26.380 --> 04:28.000
Yeah, but...

04:30.920 --> 04:32.880
Why didn't you tell me?

04:32.880 --> 04:36.630
If I was second in our grade,
I'd be bragging to everyone.

04:36.630 --> 04:40.420
School grades are nothing more than small steps.

04:41.330 --> 04:43.830
What's important is where you let them lead you.

04:44.000 --> 04:46.630
<b>School grades are nothing more than small steps.</b>

04:44.000 --> 04:46.630
<b>What's important is where you let them lead you.</b>

04:46.830 --> 04:48.630
That sounded so professional!

04:50.040 --> 04:54.170
So, you came and saw me at work, yeah?

04:54.710 --> 04:57.380
Got to see me trying my best, right?

04:58.040 --> 05:00.830
I wanna see you try.

05:05.000 --> 05:05.920
Shh!

05:08.080 --> 05:10.750
Please go out with me.

05:14.290 --> 05:16.630
Sorry, I can't.

05:18.040 --> 05:21.330
There's someone else I really like.

05:22.040 --> 05:23.210
Yamada?

05:23.960 --> 05:24.920
Yeah.

05:26.250 --> 05:28.670
You're better off dating someone else, Mita.

05:28.670 --> 05:30.540
Then why'd we go out together so much?!

05:32.790 --> 05:35.080
I don't want to see the look on her face.

05:35.080 --> 05:37.250
This guy really meant it.

05:41.250 --> 05:42.330
I'm gonna do it!

05:43.790 --> 05:45.080
The farewell address!

05:45.790 --> 05:49.420
It's time to stand proud! To let her see!

05:50.420 --> 05:51.710
To let him see...

05:53.920 --> 05:55.630
Or so I said...

05:55.920 --> 05:59.170
On behalf of all of us here,
I wish you all the best.

06:00.670 --> 06:01.920
Quit staring.

06:01.920 --> 06:04.580
You're the one who asked me to watch.

06:04.580 --> 06:07.130
You said it was the only way it counted as practice.

06:07.130 --> 06:08.040
Yeah, sorry...

06:08.670 --> 06:11.580
When did I start getting scared
of being in front of people?

06:12.380 --> 06:17.170
The award for our traffic safety poster
contest goes to Kyotaro Ichikawa.

06:17.170 --> 06:18.330
Congratulations.

06:20.290 --> 06:21.880
<b>CARS GET HURT TOO</b>

06:20.290 --> 06:21.880
<b>Stop traffic accidents</b>

06:20.290 --> 06:21.880
<b>Ah!</b>

06:20.290 --> 06:21.880
<b>Look both ways</b>

06:20.300 --> 06:21.880
<b>before crossing</b>

06:22.210 --> 06:25.670
Hah! These ignoramuses.
They're nothing compared to me.

06:26.790 --> 06:29.420
I've fallen a long way from my old self...

06:29.960 --> 06:30.920
Kyo-chan!

06:30.920 --> 06:32.210
I brought the humidifier!

06:32.210 --> 06:33.830
And the throat stuff you rub on!

06:35.290 --> 06:36.960
Okay, just rub this on your chest.

06:36.960 --> 06:39.330
This stuff is for colds.

06:39.330 --> 06:40.330
Still...

06:40.330 --> 06:43.420
I just have to read this basic script.
It's no big deal.

06:43.670 --> 06:45.960
What I need is a haircut.

06:46.170 --> 06:48.380
Okay. Will 2,000 yen do?

06:48.710 --> 06:51.250
No, I'll need 5,000 or so...

06:51.250 --> 06:52.210
What...?

06:52.880 --> 06:55.790
No way! Are you making your fancy haircut debut?!

06:57.080 --> 06:58.540
<b>Reservation Confirmed</b>

06:57.080 --> 06:58.540
<b>A confirmation email has been sent to</b>

06:57.080 --> 06:58.540
<b>your registered mail address (user ID).</b>

06:57.090 --> 06:58.540
<b>Visit your account page to make changes / cancel.</b>

06:58.710 --> 07:01.250
Great system for antisocial folks.

07:01.880 --> 07:03.000
Now, then...

07:03.670 --> 07:05.210
What are you writing?

07:05.210 --> 07:07.630
A flowchart for my conversation with the hair stylist.

07:07.630 --> 07:12.000
I need to think up easy ways to tell
them what kind of cut I want, too.

07:12.580 --> 07:16.540
<b>Hobbies - video games, Apex</b>

07:12.580 --> 07:16.540
<b>Manga - Edo Ghoul, Shukujutsu Taisen</b>

07:12.580 --> 07:16.540
<b>Movies – Pupa Effect</b>

07:12.590 --> 07:16.540
<b>Club - Data processing club,</b>

07:12.590 --> 07:16.540
<b>no club (because of cram school)</b>

07:12.590 --> 07:16.540
<b>Fresh look</b>

07:12.590 --> 07:16.540
<b>Part * No change</b>

07:12.590 --> 07:16.540
<b>Bangs * Down to eyes Sideburns * shaved, neck too</b>

07:12.920 --> 07:14.750
Want me to go with you...?

07:14.750 --> 07:16.170
I definitely don't.

07:16.630 --> 07:20.250
And so, I readied myself for the hair salon...

07:22.080 --> 07:25.170
But, they must have labeled me the non-social type,

07:25.170 --> 07:27.630
because we didn't share a word the whole time.

07:28.250 --> 07:29.830
Here's a look.

07:29.830 --> 07:31.080
Oh, thanks...

07:33.170 --> 07:36.040
These fancy places are something else.

07:36.710 --> 07:37.920
And so...

07:38.420 --> 07:41.500
My name is Kyotaro Ichikawa,
and I speak for all of us here.

07:45.960 --> 07:47.170
Quit crying!

07:47.170 --> 07:48.330
Why?

07:48.460 --> 07:52.420
<b>Meguro Ward Daijuni Junior High</b>

07:48.460 --> 07:52.420
<b>Graduation Ceremony</b>

07:48.830 --> 07:51.500
And then graduation was here.

07:57.580 --> 07:58.500
Huh?

07:58.750 --> 08:01.330
Why does this look different after just one day?

08:06.330 --> 08:07.710
Your hair's real short!

08:07.710 --> 08:09.130
You look rich!

08:09.130 --> 08:10.000
What happened?

08:10.000 --> 08:13.960
Nothing, just went to a new place and it came out weird...

08:14.210 --> 08:18.250
Yeah, make it sound like it wasn't
the first time you EVER went.

08:18.670 --> 08:20.080
You use any wax?

08:20.710 --> 08:22.000
What wax?

08:22.000 --> 08:23.130
Hang on.

08:23.750 --> 08:25.210
Hey, Adachi.

08:25.210 --> 08:26.000
Huh?

08:26.210 --> 08:28.540
You got wax on you, yeah? Hand it over.

08:28.540 --> 08:29.830
You robbing the guy?

08:33.250 --> 08:34.710
That should do it.

08:34.710 --> 08:37.210
Serina wants to be a hair stylist.

08:37.210 --> 08:40.580
I didn't say that! It's just one option.

08:41.000 --> 08:42.040
Jeez...

08:42.040 --> 08:44.880
You've got really nice hair, though.

08:45.210 --> 08:46.630
Might be able to...

08:48.580 --> 08:50.170
There! How's that?

08:50.380 --> 08:51.210
Pfff!

08:51.210 --> 08:52.250
He some thug?

08:52.580 --> 08:54.380
No one will give you crap now.

08:58.210 --> 08:59.080
Yamada...

08:59.080 --> 09:01.710
I am a model, after all.

09:04.960 --> 09:09.130
Just six months ago I never could
have imagined this situation.

09:09.540 --> 09:11.380
Enough of that, it's ribbon time.

09:11.380 --> 09:13.710
Oh yeah. UGH.

09:15.040 --> 09:16.670
What's your deal, BayashiKo?

09:24.210 --> 09:25.420
Nothing...

09:25.750 --> 09:28.790
Was just thinking how it's all over already.

09:29.750 --> 09:33.170
We're changing classes, yeah? Once we start Year 3.

09:35.000 --> 09:38.170
They say they split up groups of troublemakers.

09:38.580 --> 09:40.630
Are we troublemakers?

09:41.080 --> 09:42.540
We walk a fine line.

09:48.830 --> 09:51.080
We might get split up.

09:52.670 --> 09:54.080
We'll be fine.

09:54.960 --> 09:56.330
You know that?

09:56.330 --> 09:57.540
N-no...

09:57.880 --> 09:59.130
I don't.

09:59.130 --> 10:00.790
I don't, but...

10:02.670 --> 10:05.040
Doesn't hurt to believe it anyway.

10:07.040 --> 10:07.920
True!

10:08.830 --> 10:11.710
We're getting started. Line up in the hall.

10:11.710 --> 10:12.460
Oh...

10:15.250 --> 10:18.420
Wait, you look the same as always.

10:20.250 --> 10:22.630
Thanks, Yoshida.

10:22.630 --> 10:24.580
Huh? Nah, no worries.

10:24.580 --> 10:26.040
Let's get going.

10:26.380 --> 10:28.290
Such a pain in the butt...

10:29.130 --> 10:29.920
Those chairs literally are, too...

10:29.920 --> 10:31.250
Now then...
Those chairs literally are, too...<b></b>

10:31.580 --> 10:34.540
Just gotta make sure I have my script...

10:33.130 --> 10:35.130
<b>Hobbies - video games, Apex</b>

10:33.130 --> 10:35.130
<b>Manga - Edo Ghoul, Shukujutsu Taisen</b>

10:33.130 --> 10:35.130
<b>Movies – Pupa Effect</b>

10:33.130 --> 10:35.130
<b>Club - Data processing club,</b>

10:33.130 --> 10:35.130
<b>no club (because of cram school)</b>

10:33.130 --> 10:35.130
<b>Fresh look</b>

10:33.130 --> 10:35.130
<b>Part * No change</b>

10:33.130 --> 10:35.130
<b>Bangs * Down to eyes Sideburns * shaved, neck too</b>

10:35.250 --> 10:36.080
Huh?

10:37.380 --> 10:38.500
No...!

10:40.630 --> 10:43.830
What?! You forgot your farewell speech?!

10:44.670 --> 10:46.790
Isn't it about to start?

10:47.000 --> 10:49.170
Relax. Don't worry.

10:49.790 --> 10:52.170
I'll fly that thing there for ya!

10:52.420 --> 10:54.080
It's somewhere on your desk?

10:55.130 --> 10:57.130
I'm not gonna find any pervy stuff, am I?

10:57.130 --> 10:58.040
Just hurry!

10:58.080 --> 10:58.540
<b>Mute Mic</b>

10:58.080 --> 10:58.540
<b>Start Video</b>

10:58.540 --> 10:59.040
<b>Kana</b>

10:58.540 --> 10:59.040
<b>Voice call</b>

10:59.250 --> 11:02.330
What do I do? Do I tell the teachers I can't do it?

11:02.710 --> 11:05.000
Just stop after the opening bit I remember?

11:05.000 --> 11:06.040
Or should I...?

11:06.630 --> 11:07.750
What's up?

11:07.750 --> 11:09.330
Oh, uhh...

11:10.210 --> 11:11.580
Actually...

11:12.880 --> 11:13.960
I'm gonna do it!

11:14.540 --> 11:15.750
The farewell address!

11:17.630 --> 11:18.920
It's nothing.

11:26.790 --> 11:28.040
Ichikawa...

11:28.880 --> 11:30.170
Please...

11:30.170 --> 11:32.330
Don't tell me I can do this...

11:32.580 --> 11:33.920
Don't say it...

11:35.210 --> 11:36.210
It'll be all right.

11:39.790 --> 11:40.880
Ta-da!

11:41.500 --> 11:42.460
That's...

11:42.750 --> 11:45.540
It's mine, but you hang onto it.

11:49.170 --> 11:50.380
Now, let's go!

12:01.380 --> 12:03.580
C'mon, I gotta make it!

12:04.080 --> 12:06.040
Gah, come on!

12:07.040 --> 12:10.080
Wait, was his school this way?

12:10.670 --> 12:12.040
Something the matter?

12:12.040 --> 12:13.500
Oh, newbie!

12:13.880 --> 12:16.500
Do you happen to know Daijuni Junior High?

12:16.750 --> 12:17.960
Used to go there.

12:18.790 --> 12:21.920
Thank goodness! Can you show me the way?

12:22.080 --> 12:23.080
Follow me!

12:23.250 --> 12:24.960
C-coming!

12:28.130 --> 12:33.040
Now then, next I would like to offer a
congratulatory address from all of those here today.

12:33.580 --> 12:35.420
There's no way I can do this!

12:35.750 --> 12:38.080
A speech with no script?

12:41.830 --> 12:43.250
At this rate...

12:44.670 --> 12:47.960
My... My right arm!!!

12:48.210 --> 12:50.330
Make it stop!

12:48.210 --> 12:50.330
<b>Diploma Award Ceremony</b>

12:50.790 --> 12:53.080
No! This is a graduation!

12:53.540 --> 12:56.580
I better head over early and ask for advice.

13:01.170 --> 13:02.830
Oh, Ichikawa.

13:03.000 --> 13:03.710
Umm...

13:04.080 --> 13:07.170
Thanks for taking this on for me.

13:07.170 --> 13:07.750
Huh?

13:08.170 --> 13:11.790
I'm really grateful. Now head on that way.

13:11.790 --> 13:14.630
Hang on now! There's no way!

13:14.630 --> 13:17.580
People might be cheering me on,
but I'm still no people person!

13:17.960 --> 13:21.580
<b>CARS GET HURT TOO</b>

13:17.960 --> 13:21.580
<b>Stop traffic accidents</b>

13:17.960 --> 13:21.580
<b>Ah!</b>

13:17.960 --> 13:21.580
<b>Look both ways</b>

13:17.960 --> 13:21.580
<b>before crossing</b>

13:18.130 --> 13:19.920
That old me is gone!

13:20.290 --> 13:21.540
Quit fooling yourself.

13:23.460 --> 13:27.670
Do you think Yamada and your teachers
would cheer you on if you weren't up to this?

13:28.330 --> 13:31.580
Don't you think that old you was the real you?

13:32.040 --> 13:34.420
Who found that keychain?

13:40.670 --> 13:43.330
I'm sorry, this isn't open to the public.

13:43.330 --> 13:46.630
Listen! My brother is acting as student rep...

13:46.880 --> 13:47.830
Pretty impressive, huh?

13:47.830 --> 13:48.630
Umm...

13:48.830 --> 13:50.790
Next, a farewell address by Kyotaro Ichikawa.

13:50.790 --> 13:51.920
Agh, no!
Next, a farewell address by Kyotaro Ichikawa.<b></b>

13:51.920 --> 13:52.580
Next, a farewell address by Kyotaro Ichikawa.

13:52.580 --> 13:53.460
W-wait, stop!

13:53.670 --> 13:56.630
<b>Diploma Award Ceremony</b>

13:57.000 --> 14:01.210
Remember who trusts in you the most.

14:01.710 --> 14:02.710
Is it your teachers?

14:03.290 --> 14:04.210
Your sister?

14:04.670 --> 14:05.710
Yamada?

14:06.380 --> 14:07.460
No...

14:10.460 --> 14:11.670
It's me.

14:16.670 --> 14:17.960
You've known all along.

14:18.420 --> 14:19.130
Don't worry.

14:19.460 --> 14:20.330
It'll be all right.

14:20.580 --> 14:21.750
I can do this...

14:23.380 --> 14:25.710
The one who likes you most of all.

14:27.670 --> 14:28.710
Is ME!

14:31.380 --> 14:34.290
Don't turn your eyes from me.

14:44.380 --> 14:46.290
Farewell. The day your journey begins has come.

14:46.290 --> 14:49.250
Despite the harsh cold,
the rays of spring fall warm upon us now.

14:49.750 --> 14:54.080
I want to wish all of you celebrating
your graduation today, congratulations.

14:54.420 --> 14:56.000
We can actually hear him.

14:56.380 --> 14:59.500
We have learned much from all of you.

15:00.500 --> 15:04.210
All of us came to this school
not knowing what to expect,

15:04.210 --> 15:05.580
and you welcomed us with open arms.

15:06.330 --> 15:10.750
You leave us now as irreplaceable
parts of our lives,

15:10.750 --> 15:12.380
moving on into the future.

15:13.210 --> 15:17.920
One that may hold difficult, trying moments.

15:19.130 --> 15:21.750
But still... Even still...

15:22.420 --> 15:25.130
That's the last part I remember.

15:34.380 --> 15:38.380
But, you are the ones who must take
these steps forward yourselves!

15:38.790 --> 15:42.000
Accepting that simple fact is scary...

15:42.000 --> 15:43.000
Unthinkable.

15:43.290 --> 15:44.290
But...

15:45.210 --> 15:46.920
But, you can't run away from it!

15:47.420 --> 15:51.130
Because, you have already seen the light!

15:53.290 --> 15:55.000
It is in your friends.

15:55.000 --> 15:56.170
Your teachers.

15:56.710 --> 15:59.040
And in all you've experienced in this place of learning.

15:59.500 --> 16:01.210
Who's the one graduating, here?

16:02.580 --> 16:04.830
It will be all right.

16:06.210 --> 16:08.170
Don't give up trying new things.

16:08.500 --> 16:10.330
Learn to love yourselves.

16:11.130 --> 16:12.920
Treasure all that you have come to know.

16:13.670 --> 16:20.710
My name is Kyotaro Ichikawa,
and I speak on behalf of the student body.

16:36.830 --> 16:38.540
That was great, Ichikawa!

16:38.960 --> 16:42.460
Those ignoramuses.
They were nothing compared to me.

16:43.790 --> 16:46.130
Ichikawa? Ichikawa?!

16:48.790 --> 16:50.750
<b>Nurse's Office</b>

16:51.540 --> 16:54.630
Guess I'm still me in the end.

16:55.460 --> 16:56.210
How do you feel?

16:56.210 --> 16:58.920
I-I'm fine already.

17:00.630 --> 17:01.630
You know...

17:02.420 --> 17:03.960
Your farewell speech...

17:03.960 --> 17:06.250
Good. There you are.

17:06.250 --> 17:07.290
Senpai-Pick Up Artist...

17:07.290 --> 17:09.880
Oh, and our student rep is here, too.

17:09.880 --> 17:11.880
That speech was awesome.

17:11.880 --> 17:13.580
Pulled on the heartstrings.

17:13.580 --> 17:15.630
Emptier words were never spoken.

17:15.960 --> 17:18.920
So, Yamada. You got a minute?

17:20.250 --> 17:21.290
Yamada.

17:23.830 --> 17:25.290
I'm gonna sleep for a bit.

17:27.580 --> 17:29.380
We can just talk here.

17:34.920 --> 17:37.250
Congratulations on graduating.

17:37.250 --> 17:38.330
Thanks.

17:38.330 --> 17:40.290
If he pulls anything weird...

17:40.580 --> 17:41.460
It's this...

17:41.460 --> 17:42.460
This...

17:42.460 --> 17:43.460
And this!

17:44.750 --> 17:49.460
I'm not the same me from back then.

17:51.000 --> 17:54.580
So, are you going to keep playing soccer in high school?

17:54.580 --> 17:56.250
Huh? Why would you ask?

17:56.750 --> 18:00.750
I always saw you watching them
practice even after you left the club.

18:01.420 --> 18:03.790
Figured you must like soccer.

18:08.830 --> 18:12.040
Happy to hear you took that much notice.

18:13.000 --> 18:14.540
"Hold it right there!"

18:15.380 --> 18:17.000
Is that what you're thinking?

18:18.250 --> 18:19.210
Not really...

18:19.880 --> 18:22.380
This is all just some empty ritual.

18:23.630 --> 18:27.210
I was on the youth team back in elementary school.

18:27.630 --> 18:30.380
But, sticking with it doesn't guarantee you can go pro.

18:30.380 --> 18:31.880
And it's more fun just playing around.

18:33.250 --> 18:35.750
You're impressive, in that way.

18:36.000 --> 18:37.920
Heard you're in movies now.

18:37.920 --> 18:39.960
You're way cooler than me.

18:40.670 --> 18:43.960
Makes me happy to see you working hard.

18:43.960 --> 18:45.040
I respect you for it.

18:45.460 --> 18:46.830
Same as me...

18:46.830 --> 18:48.420
No, that's not it...

18:48.420 --> 18:49.750
It's not?

18:53.790 --> 18:54.830
I like you.

19:01.670 --> 19:04.460
I want you to have my uniform button.

19:11.750 --> 19:12.830
I know how you feel!

19:13.080 --> 19:13.830
Huh?

19:13.830 --> 19:15.460
No, I mean...

19:15.460 --> 19:18.210
How it makes you happy to
see someone working hard.

19:18.210 --> 19:21.830
How you respect them and are
afraid they'll start to hate you,

19:21.830 --> 19:23.420
so you get all worried...

19:23.420 --> 19:24.790
And that's why...

19:25.290 --> 19:27.580
Well, I mean...

19:28.000 --> 19:30.170
I... Umm...

19:33.170 --> 19:36.750
There's someone else I like!

19:39.790 --> 19:41.710
So, I'm sorry...

19:43.330 --> 19:47.130
My hands are full,
and I can't hold anything else.

19:53.290 --> 19:55.000
I know how it feels...

19:55.880 --> 19:58.670
To cry over someone you like...

19:59.920 --> 20:00.830
Yamada...

20:01.330 --> 20:02.500
Yamada...

20:03.210 --> 20:05.170
<b>Yamada</b>

20:06.880 --> 20:08.330
...likes me...

20:11.960 --> 20:14.630
<b>Likes Me</b>

20:18.710 --> 20:21.290
Okay. Graduation's over for me.

20:21.960 --> 20:22.710
See ya.

20:27.170 --> 20:29.380
I'll message you over spring break.

20:29.380 --> 20:30.080
Huh?

20:30.460 --> 20:36.040
Our little student rep friend gave
me your info when I asked him.

20:36.290 --> 20:37.920
Wha?! No, I...!

20:37.920 --> 20:38.790
That's not true.

20:40.500 --> 20:43.460
Don't lie to me like that.

20:45.710 --> 20:47.380
Not fallin' for it, huh?

20:53.830 --> 20:56.290
<b>Yamada Likes Me</b>

20:59.290 --> 21:02.630
Why leave with a lie that makes her hate you like that?

21:03.670 --> 21:05.750
Why didn't you tell her you quit
soccer because you got hurt?

21:05.750 --> 21:08.540
Then she'd only love me out of sympathy.

21:13.290 --> 21:16.080
Slow down now, you were finally alone!

21:17.040 --> 21:17.920
Huh?

21:26.460 --> 21:27.710
Uh... what?

21:28.250 --> 21:31.000
Did they do it in those few seconds they had?

21:31.000 --> 21:32.540
Seriously, right?
